Maintainer: akashmony01 <akashmony01@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, libportaudio2, wl-clipboard, xclip, pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/akashmony01/FloatNote
Description: hold a key, talk, get a bug list for Claude Code
 FloatNote records short voice notes while you test an app: hold Ctrl+Super,
 describe the problem, let go. Speech is transcribed on your computer with
 faster-whisper. When you're done, one key copies all notes as a numbered list
 to paste into Claude Code, or Claude Code reads them with `floatnote list`.
 .
 Installing downloads FloatNote's Python libraries from PyPI into
 /usr/lib/floatnote/venv; the speech model (~460 MB) is downloaded on first
 start. Built for Ubuntu 24.04 or newer with GNOME.
